        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Sangam-age Tamilakam</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">Tamilakam, “home of Tamil”: today’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>, Puducherry, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshadweep">Lakshadweep</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>; cities <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uraiyur">Uraiyur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puhar">Puhar</a>; ports <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korkai">Korkai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muziris">Muziris</a>; the excavated site of Keezhadi</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Usually c. 300 BCE–300 CE; Kamil Zvelebil finds 100 BCE–250 CE most acceptable for the poems; some accounts begin the age c. 600 BCE, and Keezhadi is radiocarbon-dated to the 6th century BCE; post-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangam-literature">Sangam literature</a> c. 250–600 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Sangam poetry of love (akam) and war (puram); the Tolkappiyam grammar; the three crowned dynasties, Chera, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a>; the Velir chieftains; pearls, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> and textiles; sea trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">2,381 Sangam poems by 473 poets; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-brahmi">Tamil-Brahmi</a> and other inscriptions, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>’s and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharavela">Kharavela</a>’s; Greek and Roman writers (the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/periplus-of-the-erythraean-sea">Periplus</a>, Pliny, Ptolemy); Roman coins and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amphora">amphorae</a>; excavations such as Keezhadi</span></div>
        </div>
